--TEST--
a string argument at a parameter typed `property<T>` alone is offered the public properties of `T`, because the checker converts that literal to a key while compiling — `rule:ide/completion-offers-only-what-the-compiler-derived`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Order {
    public string $id = "o1";
    public int $total = 3;
    private string $note = "x";
}
class Grid {
    public static function sortBy(property<Order> $column): string {
        return $column as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::sortBy("<|>");
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
id      property  string
total   property  int
